{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Current Gap\n\nStories 1934, 749c, 1fd4, and 0b14 landed the authenticated `undeclared`, `paths`, and `none` behavior. Current-state inspection shows that the standalone gate, ticket-model, and event-schema docs do not yet describe the complete tri-state contract, and the public `rebar explain plan` author guide does not yet explain the truthful `set-file-impact --none` workflow. This ticket creates that missing documentation. Because it edits repository files, its own scope is `paths`, never `none`.\n\n## Execution Steps\n\n1. Update `docs/plan-review-gate.md` with an explicit tri-state section. Define each state and freshness effect; live-child neutral/poison roll-up; closed-child exclusion; declaration changes in the material fingerprint; and a mixed `paths` plus `none` example.\n2. Update `docs/ticket-model.md` beside file impact with the same three persisted states, and state that docs-only and test-only work still touches repository files and therefore declares `paths`.\n3. Reconcile `docs/event-schema.md` FILE_IMPACT wording with the landed event keys and transitions among `undeclared`, `paths`, and `none`, including which fields are cleared on each transition.\n4. Update `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md`, the packaged source for the public `rebar explain plan` command. Explain when `set-file-impact --none` is truthful, that docs-only/test-only work is not none, and that the no-file-impact LLM criterion requires a substantive reason covering both why no repository file changes occur and where the output or evidence lives.\n5. RED-first, add `test_explain_plan_file_impact_tristate_contract` in `tests/unit/test_plan_review_explain.py`. Invoke the public CLI entry point `main([\"explain\", \"plan\"])`, capture stdout, and assert the rendered user-facing contract communicates the three choices, the `set-file-impact --none` command, the repository-file meaning of none, the docs-only/test-only counterexample, and the two-part substantive-reason requirement. Assertions may target the public output contract but must remain insensitive to paragraph wording, source layout, headings, and ordering. The test must not read or grep source files, inspect private implementation shape, or snapshot exact formatting.\n6. Verify the three standalone docs with an operator semantic checklist against the acceptance criteria below and record the completed checklist as a ticket comment. These docs are not exercised through a runtime entry point, so this verification is intentionally manual and semantic; do not add grep-based, source-text, snapshot, or formatting/order tests for them.\n7. Run the focused RED/GREEN test, perform a defect-seeded mutation/teeth check against the packaged guide behavior, apply the refactoring litmus, then run `make lint`, the project typecheck gate, and the full test suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` defines `undeclared` as whole-HEAD freshness, `paths` as dependency-scoped freshness, and authenticated `none` as contributing no file dependencies.\n- [ ] The gate doc states live `none` children are neutral, live undeclared children poison inheritance, and closed children are ignored.\n- [ ] The gate doc states declaration changes alter the material fingerprint and includes a mixed-scope example where a `paths` child contributes dependencies while a `none` child does not.\n- [ ] `docs/ticket-model.md` documents all three persisted states beside file impact and states docs-only/test-only work uses `paths`, not `none`.\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md` documents `file_impact`, `file_impact_scope`, and `no_file_impact_reason`, plus field-clearing semantics for transitions among all three states.\n- [ ] Public `rebar explain plan` output communicates the three choices and the `set-file-impact --none` command.\n- [ ] Public `rebar explain plan` output states that none means no repository file is touched and docs-only/test-only work uses `paths`.\n- [ ] Public `rebar explain plan` output states that a none claim is LLM-reviewed and its substantive reason explains both why no repository file changes occur and where output/evidence lives.\n- [ ] `test_explain_plan_file_impact_tristate_contract` exercises the public CLI output and contains no source-file reads, source grep, private-shape assertions, exact-paragraph snapshots, or formatting/order assertions.\n- [ ] A ticket comment records the operator semantic checklist for all standalone-doc acceptance criteria.\n- [ ] No production logic or schema files change; under `src/rebar`, only `_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md` changes.\n- [ ] `make lint`, typecheck, and the full test suite pass."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785262824851089001,"uuid":"e54bdaf6-cd81-4f44-a2de-18d3055d1c49"}